module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.ProjInvertibleTwistRelativeUnit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.ProjInvertibleTwistRelativeCanonical
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.Comparison

/-!
# Tag 02NC over a base scheme: the chart comparison does not depend on the trivializing section

Tag 02NC asserts that its isomorphism is **canonical**, and its proof glues the comparisons
attached to the members of a covering of the base over which `ℒ` is trivialized. For that glueing
to be possible the comparison over one open must not depend on the section chosen there. This
file proves exactly that, as an equality of morphisms of homogeneous spectra:

`Proj.map (ψ_{x'}) = Proj.map (ψ_x)` whenever `x' = u · x` for a unit `u` of the functions on the
open.

Two sections of `ℒ` trivializing it over the same open do differ by such a unit —
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorGenerator.exists_unit_smul_generator` — so this is the canonicity the
glueing consumes, and it is the relative analogue of
`Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.projTwist_eq_of_generators`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeInvertibleTwist.irrelevant_le_map_psiSectionAt`: **Mathlib's
  hypothesis for `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map`** holds for the chart comparison as soon as the
  powers of the section trivialize the powers of `ℒ` in every positive degree. This is what lets
  the chart comparison be written as `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` rather than only as the partial
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistChain.mapHom`; it is this input, and not
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.mapHomOfTop_eq_map`, that the comparison needs.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeInvertibleTwist.projMap_psiSectionAt`: the chart comparison
  as a morphism `Proj ℬ(V) ⟶ Proj 𝒜(V)` of homogeneous spectra.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeInvertibleTwist.projMap_psiSectionAt_eq_of_unit_smul`:
  **the comparison is unchanged by rescaling the section by a unit.**
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeInvertibleTwist.projMap_psiSectionAt_eq_mapHomOfTop`: the
  comparison agrees with the partial `mapHom` of
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeInvertibleTwist.isIso_mapHom_psiSectionAt`, so the
  isomorphism proved there is an isomorphism of this morphism too.

## Why the hypothesis is `∀ d, 0 < d` and not `∀ᶠ d`

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjChain.isIso_mapHom_of_eventually_bijective` is content with
bijectivity in all sufficiently large degrees, because the homogeneous spectrum only sees the
large degrees. Mathlib's hypothesis `ℬ₊ ≤ 𝒜₊.map ψ` is not: it asks of **every** homogeneous
element of positive degree that it lie in the ideal generated by the images, and an element of a
small degree is not reached from the large ones, the span being taken in the ring and not in the
graded pieces. So the hypothesis here is the trivialization in every positive degree, which is
what a section trivializing `ℒ` supplies anyway.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02NC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Filter Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistChain
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedAlgebraTwist

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeInvertibleTwist

attribute [local instance] Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓ
  Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓSheaf Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsSMulCommClassΓ
  Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓPresheaf
  Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓSheafPresheaf
  Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓSheafVal

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (L : S.Modules)
  [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.sheaf.obj S.ringCatSheaf.property L]
  (𝒜 : SheafGradedAlgebra S)

/-- **Mathlib's hypothesis for `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` holds for the chart comparison.**

A homogeneous element of the twist of positive degree `d` is `ψ` of a homogeneous element of `𝒜`
of the same degree, because the comparison is bijective on the degree-`d` sections as soon as the
`d`-th power of the section trivializes the `d`-th tensor power of `ℒ`; so it lies in the ideal
generated by the images outright, with no localization and no radical. -/
theorem irrelevant_le_map_psiSectionAt {V : S.Opens} {x : (tp L 1).val.obj (op V)}
    (hx : ∀ d : ℕ, 0 < d → TrivializesPower L V x d) :
    HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant ((twist 𝒜 L).grading V) ≤
      (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (𝒜.grading V)).map (psiSectionAt L 𝒜 V x) := by
  refine irrelevant_le_map_of_mem_span _ _ _ fun d hd g hg => ?_
  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hg
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := (bijective_psiPieceAt_of_trivializesPower L 𝒜 (hx d hd)).surjective b
  refine Ideal.subset_span ⟨DirectSum.of (𝒜.sectionPieces V) d a,
    Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨d, Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨hd, 𝒜.of_mem_grading V a⟩⟩, ?_⟩
  exact (psiSectionAt_of L 𝒜 V x a).trans
    (congrArg (DirectSum.of ((twist 𝒜 L).sectionPieces V) d) ha)

/-- **The chart comparison of Tag 02NC as a morphism of homogeneous spectra**,
`Proj ℬ(V) ⟶ Proj 𝒜(V)`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` of the comparison homomorphism of graded rings attached to a
section of `ℒ` over `V` whose powers trivialize the powers of `ℒ` there. For `V` an affine open
of the base the two spectra are the preimages of `V` in `Proj_S(ℬ)` and `Proj_S(𝒜)` by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwistQcoh.chartIsoPreimage`, so this is the tag's `g` over
that chart. -/
def projMap_psiSectionAt {V : S.Opens} {x : (tp L 1).val.obj (op V)}
    (hx : ∀ d : ℕ, 0 < d → TrivializesPower L V x d) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj ((twist 𝒜 L).grading V) ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (𝒜.grading V) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map (psiSectionAt L 𝒜 V x) (irrelevant_le_map_psiSectionAt L 𝒜 hx)

/-- **The chart comparison does not depend on the trivializing section**: rescaling the section by
a unit of the functions on the open leaves the morphism of homogeneous spectra unchanged.

Rescaling the section rescales the degree-`d` component of the comparison by the `d`-th power of
the image of the unit under the structure map
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeInvertibleTwist.psiSectionAt_smul_of`), which is a degree
scaling by an invertible element of degree zero, and such a rescaling induces the identity on the
homogeneous spectrum.

Two sections trivializing `ℒ` over `V` differ by such a unit
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorGenerator.exists_unit_smul_generator`), so this is the canonicity
that the glueing of Tag 02NC over a trivializing covering of the base consumes on overlaps. It is
the relative analogue of `Stacks.GradedRing.InvertibleTwist.projTwist_eq_of_generators`. -/
theorem projMap_psiSectionAt_eq_of_unit_smul {V : S.Opens} (u : (funsAt V)ˣ)
    {x x' : (tp L 1).val.obj (op V)} (hu : x' = (u : funsAt V) • x)
    (hx : ∀ d : ℕ, 0 < d → TrivializesPower L V x d)
    (hx' : ∀ d : ℕ, 0 < d → TrivializesPower L V x' d) :
    projMap_psiSectionAt L 𝒜 hx' = projMap_psiSectionAt L 𝒜 hx := by
  subst hu
  refine Stacks.GradedRing.Proj_map_eq_of_target_degreeScale _
    ((twist 𝒜 L).strHom_mem V (u : funsAt V))
    ((twist 𝒜 L).strHom_mem V ((u⁻¹ : (funsAt V)ˣ) : funsAt V)) ?_ _ _ _ _ fun i a ha => ?_
  · exact ((twist 𝒜 L).strHom V).map_mul (u : funsAt V) ((u⁻¹ : (funsAt V)ˣ) : funsAt V) ▸
      (congrArg ((twist 𝒜 L).strHom V) u.mul_inv).trans (map_one ((twist 𝒜 L).strHom V))
  · obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := ha
    exact psiSectionAt_smul_of L 𝒜 (u : funsAt V) x y

/-- **The chart comparison is the partial `mapHom` of the chart isomorphism.**

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeInvertibleTwist.isIso_mapHom_psiSectionAt` states the chart
comparison to be an isomorphism for `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistChain.mapHom`, the morphism
out of the domain of definition `U(ψ)`; here the domain is everything, and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.mapHomOfTop_eq_map` identifies the resulting morphism of
spectra with `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map`. So the isomorphism proved there is an isomorphism of
the morphism this file is about. -/
theorem mapHomOfTop_psiSectionAt_eq_projMap {V : S.Opens} {x : (tp L 1).val.obj (op V)}
    (hx : ∀ d : ℕ, 0 < d → TrivializesPower L V x d)
    (hdom : mapDomain (𝒜.grading V) ((twist 𝒜 L).grading V) (psiSectionAt L 𝒜 V x) = ⊤) :
    mapHomOfTop (𝒜.grading V) ((twist 𝒜 L).grading V) (psiSectionAt L 𝒜 V x) hdom =
      projMap_psiSectionAt L 𝒜 hx :=
  mapHomOfTop_eq_map _ _ _ (irrelevant_le_map_psiSectionAt L 𝒜 hx) hdom

/-- The domain of definition of the chart comparison is everything, from the trivialization in
every positive degree alone: Mathlib's hypothesis implies it. -/
theorem mapDomain_psiSectionAt_eq_top' {V : S.Opens} {x : (tp L 1).val.obj (op V)}
    (hx : ∀ d : ℕ, 0 < d → TrivializesPower L V x d) :
    mapDomain (𝒜.grading V) ((twist 𝒜 L).grading V) (psiSectionAt L 𝒜 V x) = ⊤ :=
  mapDomain_eq_top_of_irrelevant_le_map _ _ _ (irrelevant_le_map_psiSectionAt L 𝒜 hx)

/-- **The chart comparison is an isomorphism of homogeneous spectra.**
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeInvertibleTwist.isIso_mapHom_psiSectionAt` transported along
`mapHomOfTop_psiSectionAt_eq_projMap`. -/
theorem isIso_projMap_psiSectionAt {V : S.Opens} {x : (tp L 1).val.obj (op V)}
    (hx : ∀ d : ℕ, 0 < d → TrivializesPower L V x d) :
    IsIso (projMap_psiSectionAt L 𝒜 hx) := by
  have heventually : ∀ᶠ d : ℕ in atTop, TrivializesPower L V x d :=
    eventually_atTop.mpr ⟨1, fun d hd => hx d hd⟩
  have := isIso_mapHom_psiSectionAt L 𝒜 heventually
  rw [← mapHomOfTop_psiSectionAt_eq_projMap L 𝒜 hx (mapDomain_psiSectionAt_eq_top' L 𝒜 hx)]
  unfold mapHomOfTop
  infer_instance

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeInvertibleTwist

end
